eter of various shapes", "conf": 0.879, "box": [[242, 808], [1550, 811], [1550, 848], [242, 845]]}, {"text": "using formula.", "conf": 0.859, "box": [[242, 857], [459, 857], [459, 894], [242, 894]]}, {"text": "8.1Perimeter", "conf": 0.87, "box": [[734, 935], [1043, 939], [1042, 982], [734, 978]]}, {"text": "Previous KnowledgeCheck", "conf": 0.881, "box": [[1136, 966], [1543, 972], [1542, 1005], [1136, 999]]}, {"text": "We know that perimeter of a shape is measured by adding", "conf": 0.894, "box": [[173, 1020], [1090, 1035], [1089, 1074], [172, 1059]]}, {"text": "Howcanwefindthespace", "conf": 0.938, "box": [[1193, 1025], [1538, 1031], [1537, 1061], [1193, 1055]]}, {"text": "the length of all its sides. Its always measured in single units", "conf": 0.903, "box": [[173, 1072], [1102, 1086], [1101, 1122], [172, 1108]]}, {"text": "covered byacupboard ina", "conf": 0.885, "box": [[1193, 1066], [1543, 1070], [1542, 1100], [1193, 1096]]}, {"text": "room?", "conf": 0.804, "box": [[1192, 1106], [1280, 1106], [1280, 1133], [1192, 1133]]}, {"text": "i.e. centimetres (cm), metres (m), etc.", "conf": 0.868, "box": [[173, 1121], [734, 1131], [733, 1166], [172, 1156]]}, {"text": "How can we find the length", "conf": 0.868, "box": [[1191, 1140], [1547, 1147], [1546, 1179], [1191, 1172]]}, {"text": "of the boundary wall around", "conf": 0.868, "box": [[1193, 1178], [1560, 1186], [1559, 1219], [1193, 1211]]}, {"text": "8.1.1Perimeter of square", "conf": 0.892, "box": [[175, 1192], [651, 1203], [650, 1239], [174, 1228]]}, {"text": "the playground?", "conf": 0.914, "box": [[1193, 1217], [1405, 1221], [1404, 1255], [1193, 1251]]}, {"text": "A square is a four sided 2-D shape having all sides equal in length. Its perimeter Length", "conf": 0.907, "box": [[172, 1243], [1539, 1285], [1537, 1340], [170, 1298]]}, {"text": "can be measure by adding all 4 sides. If L is the length of a side of the square,", "conf": 0.933, "box": [[177, 1304], [1389, 1332], [1388, 1371], [176, 1343]]}, {"text"